#!/bin/sh
# Fetch Tom Harte's 6502 SingleStepTests (10,000 cases an opcode, before and
# after, every bus cycle; MIT) for the opcodes the CPU implements, into
# target/harte/, where `cargo test harte` runs them. About 640 MB.
set -e
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
mkdir -p target/harte
opcodes=$(grep -oE "0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{2} => Some" src/instructions/op_codes.rs | cut -c3-4 | tr 'A-F' 'a-f' | sort -u)
for op in $opcodes; do
    [ -s "target/harte/$op.json" ] || curl -sSfL -o "target/harte/$op.json" \
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SingleStepTests/65x02/main/6502/v1/$op.json"
done
echo "target/harte: $(ls target/harte | wc -l) opcodes; cargo test harte -- --nocapture"
